titre$ANDERS MUNK DANISH PYRENOMYCETES clé générale
com$ANDERS MUNK DANSK BOTANISK ARKIV, UDGIVET AF DANSK BOTANISK FORENING Bind 17 N°1/ adapt GF 07/2013
Bind 17 N°1 DANSK BOTANISK ARKIV, UDGIVET AF DANSK BOTANISK FORENING, 
 rem$LANGUE$Anglais

µm           ±

SACCARDO'S artificial "sporologicat" system of the Pyrenomycetes has been
adopted here as a basis for construction of the following artificial key to the Danish
genera of Pyrenomycetes. The groups within this system arc characterised as
follows:
1,cs1 $ Spores ± sausage-shaped, hyaline or slightly coloured, not septate (or with an indistinct median plasmatic separation of the contents).The coloured allantoid spores are often ± flattened. $ Allantosporae$s"Allantosporae"
1,cs5 $ Spores ellipsoid or fusiform, hyaline, not septate. $ Hyalosporae $s"Hyalosporae"
1,cs8 $ Spores ellipsoid or fusiform, coloured, not septate. - Several Phaeosporae have hyaline appendages (of various morphological value) on the spores. $ Phaeosporae $s""
1,cs15 $ Spores hyaline, composed of two cells when mature. $ Hyalodidymae $s"Hyalodidymae"
1,cs18$ Spores coloured, composed of two cells when mature. $ Phaeodidymae $s"Phaeodidymae"
1,cs23$ Spores hyalines, transversally septate, composed of more than two cells. $ Hyalophragmae $s"Hyalophragmae"
1,cs27$ Spores coloured, transversally septate, composed of more than two cells. $ Phaeophragmae $s"Phaeophragmae"
1,cs30 $ Spores both transversally and longitudinally septate. $ Dictyosporae $s"Dictyosporae "
1,cs35 $ Spores very long and thin, often perfectly filiform, hyaline or slightly coloured, generally ± indistinctly transversally septate. Swollen cells may occur $ Scolecosporae $s"Scolecosporae"
........................

